    verification rejectIsHumanJudgedWhereAnAcceptanceIsRefineGate : Test { :>> id = "eae82b81-055b-43d8-986e-067db65c1f6f"; :>> title = "Sprint 702 refine gate (DoR)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::inspect; :>> procedureText = "Chartered by issue526's governing Decision (this sprint's co-committed safety-change, proposed): an AI actor could record a human's rejection with nothing refusing it at the write, in the command lists or in the rule, while the reject command's synopsis claimed accept's channel rules. Two points: one call inside the lock, two list entries, one guard loop, one rule, one test. DoR: dcRejectIsHumanJudgedAtTheWriteAndTheRule ranks second on keel show whats-next after sprint 701's reorder placed it in the High band (D0052); the pair is the DoD's own, named before the patch was applied; the two rejected Decisions in the tree (d0376, d0463, grep DecisionStatus::rejected over .engine/decisions) each carry a RejectR1 judged by the human, so the new blocking rule evaluates over two subjects with zero violators and needs no backfill (migration skill gate 4 not engaged); the draft first claimed zero rejected Decisions from a grep over .tracking alone - the rule's own scanned count (keel gate rules: evaluated, 0 violations; guard confirmation-authenticity 460 = 458 accepted + 2 rejected) corrected it before commit."; }
