    verification rejectIsHumanJudgedWhereAnAcceptanceIsRetroGate : Test { :>> id = "36d322ec-8668-4f11-9340-a01f7362276f"; :>> title = "Sprint 702 retro gate (autonomous, D0049)"; :>> createdAt = "2026-09-13"; :>> createdBy = "claudeFable5"; :>> method = VerificationMethod::analyze; :>> procedureText = "Finding: the control_structure test human_authority_commands_refuse_an_ai_actor holds every listed command to the write layer, but a command listed in neither list is invisible to it - issue526 sat there for five days. The structural fix is a test in the other direction: every CliCommand whose synopsis or family claims the human's verdict (accept, reject, judge-set today) must appear in HUMAN_AUTHORITY_COMMANDS; that is a claim about the CLI facts (D0271) held to code, the same shape as the write-path registry. Tracked as issue529 (resolver dcVerdictCommandsAreReadBackIntoTheAuthorityLists, Medium band), not fixed here (one clause per sprint, D0303). D0131 avoidable-issue scan: issue526 was avoidable at D0393 by reading reject's write path when its synopsis was given accept's words; no further item. Second finding: the refine text and D0470's context first said no Decision had ever been rejected, from a grep over .tracking when Decisions live in .engine/decisions; the rule this sprint adds scanned two (d0376, d0463) and so falsified the claim before commit. No item: no automated control reads a prose count, and the correction is D0151's - the check (here, the rule's scanned count) runs before the claim is written. Third finding: the VERIFIER's receipt read the touched run as MISMATCH because the test-verify skill's stems row (SKILL.md:126) predates the embedded init stem (touched.rs:16) that every changed .engine path contributes - a correct receipt over this sprint's rules.sysml change reported as dishonest. Tracked as issue530 (resolver dcTouchedReceiptStatesItsOwnAttribution, Medium band): the receipt states its own attribution so the reader compares against the receipt, not a re-derived rule."; }
